// -- Assemble and register -----------------------------------------------------
// Vertical alignment for ELA. Derived, not scraped -- and the reason is worth
// knowing. TEA's ELAR strand charts show the SAME LETTER carrying across every
// grade with only the verb escalating: "(A) make and confirm predictions" is
// word-for-word identical from Kindergarten to English IV. So the alignment is
// one-to-one and mechanical.
//
// What is NOT mechanical, and is the whole value here, is that the SECTION
// NUMBER changes between grade bands. Comprehension is x.6 in grades 3-5, x.5
// in grades 6-8 and x.4 at EOC. A Grade 6 teacher reading 6.10.B has no way to
// guess last year's was 5.11.B. 84 of these renumberings exist.
//
// Joined on TEA's own knowledge-and-skills names, not on our strand column:
// "Composition" covers TWO sections (writing process and composition genres),
// so joining on the strand matched 4.11.B to 3.12.B -- the wrong one.
