/**
 * TEK DESCRIPTOR TEXT  --  reference data, paste once and leave alone.
 *
 * A separate Apps Script file on purpose. It is 130 KB of static lookup that
 * changes only when TEA changes the standards, and the main file is copied by
 * hand every time we alter logic -- there is no reason to move this with it.
 * Apps Script shares one global scope across files, so these are visible to
 * the analyser exactly as if they sat in it.
 *
 * CONTENT: the descriptor and the Readiness/Supporting designation are TEA's
 * published standards. They are extracted from the lead4ward IQ exports, which
 * reproduce TEA's wording; none of lead4ward's own analysis, cluster naming or
 * vocabulary work is included here.
 *
 * FORMAT: "R|text", "S|text" or "|text" -- one string per TEK rather than an
 * object, to keep a large table small.
 *
 * Spanish is a SEPARATE table, never a fallback. Grades 4 and 5 share TEK codes
 * across ELAR and SLAR but not wording -- one reads "standard English
 * conventions", the other "standard Spanish" -- and the Spanish maths
 * descriptors are written in Spanish throughout. Falling back would put the
 * wrong language, and sometimes the wrong standard, in front of a teacher.
 */

