// ================================================================================================
// PART 3: Ref_Cut_Scores  --  TEA performance-level cut scores, by year
// (source: reference_src/Ref_Cut_Scores.gs)
// ================================================================================================

/**
 * TEA's six enhanced performance levels, by year, grade, subject and language.\n *\n * REPLACED EVERY YEAR. The Approaches, Meets and Masters cuts are standing\n * standards; only the two interior cuts move, because TEA recalculates them\n * from the prior distribution.
 *
 * REFERENCE DATA -- no logic. Paste once into the Apps Script project and leave
 * it alone; the analyser is the only file that gets re-pasted when we change
 * how anything works.
 *
 * Apps Script shares one global scope across every .gs in a project, so these
 * are visible to the analyser exactly as if they sat inside it. Nothing here
 * runs at load time and nothing here depends on file order.
 */


// TEA "enhanced performance levels" -- the six bands the A-F School Progress
// domain uses, keyed by accountability year then grade|subject|language.
//
// Source: TEA's annual "Raw Scores and Scale Scores Associated with the
// Calculation of School Progress, Part A: Academic Growth". Both years are here
// because growth compares a pupil's PRIOR-year band with their CURRENT-year
// band, and TEA re-publishes the cuts every year.
//
// Ranges are SCALE score. TEA says the levels are determined by raw score, and
// prints raw too -- but the EOC file gives raw as "Varies", because a course has
// several administrations on different forms. Scale is the only key that works
// for every assessment, and the export carries it.
//
// The ranges have deliberate gaps (a band may end 1536 and the next begin 1554)
// because scale scores are discrete. So banding uses LOWER BOUNDS: the band is
// the last one whose floor the score reaches. A raw score of zero is excluded
// from growth entirely and never reaches this table.
