// ================================================================================================
// PART 6: Ref_State_Averages  --  State percent correct per TEK (derived from lead4ward exports)
// (source: reference_src/Ref_State_Averages.gs)
// ================================================================================================

/**
 * State percentage of pupils correct, per TEK, per year.\n *\n * REPLACED EVERY YEAR, when the new STAAR administration is published. That is\n * why it is a file of its own: nothing else in the project changes on that\n * cadence, and swapping it should never mean re-pasting logic.
 *
 * REFERENCE DATA -- no logic. Paste once into the Apps Script project and leave
 * it alone; the analyser is the only file that gets re-pasted when we change
 * how anything works.
 *
 * Apps Script shares one global scope across every .gs in a project, so these
 * are visible to the analyser exactly as if they sat inside it. Nothing here
 * runs at load time and nothing here depends on file order.
 */


// Rebuilt 31 Aug 2026 from the lead4ward IQ Tool PDFs, English forms only.
// Shape: { tek: { year: { pct, q, n } } }.  `q` only when one item carried that
// TEK that year; `n` is how many items were averaged.
//
// `pct` is MEAN PERCENT OF POINTS EARNED, matching classPct (earned/possible)
// which every view compares it against. For a 2-point item that is
// full + partial/2 -- partial on a 2-pointer is exactly one of two points.
// Storing bare full-credit % understated those items by 15 points on average.
//
// Two faults in the previous table, both fixed here:
//   1. It was extracted one item per page. On any page holding two items the
//      second was dropped, and a griddable's percentage was read off the
//      multiple-choice item beside it. 161 of 945 figures were wrong, mean
//      error 12 points, worst 67 -> 13.
//   2. Partial credit was ignored (see above).
// Verified: every multiple-choice option set in the source sums to ~100, and
